    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions\">Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions</a></i> </p><p>Most <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Anarrians\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Anarrians\">Anarrians</a> are citizens of The Anarrian Empire, the government that reigns over the planet's western continent and many of the islands nearby. Since its inception around the time of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"The Mandalorian Wars\">The Mandalorian Wars</a>, the Empire has fought to gain dominance over <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/The_Altirian_Republic\" title=\"The Altirian Republic\">The Altirian Republic</a> and establish its rule over Anarris. </p><p>Thanks to their perpetual state of military readiness and training, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Anarrians\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Anarrians\">Anarrians</a> are prepared to launch an assault on any who stand in their way, including rogue cells of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Anarrians\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Anarrians\">Anarrians</a> who choose other philosophies and goals. </p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Anarrian_Heroic_Units\">Anarrian Heroic Units</span></h2><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heroic_Units\" title=\"Heroic Units\">Heroic Units</a></i> </p><table class=\"wikitable\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <th>NAME </th> \n   <th>CHALLENGE LEVEL </th> \n   <th>AFFILIATION NOTES </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <th colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Unknown_Regions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Unknown Regions\">Unknown Regions</a> </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Dilta\" title=\"Dilta\">Dilta</a> </td> \n   <td>CL 0 </td> \n   <td>Unlike most <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Anarrian\" title=\"Anarrian\">Anarrian</a> children, Dilta likes to break away from groups to venture out on his own, mainly to explore Rastar and see what the city holds. </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table>",
